      "rev_n_16_cf57de_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_16_cf57de_1",
        "node_id": "n_16_cf57de",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous implementation was due to the game ending prematurely after only one second. To fix this, we need to modify the simulation loop to continue until either all bacteria reach the trap or a collision occurs. Here's a revised thought process:\n\nInstead of treating all bacteria as moving simultaneously and checking for collisions at the end of each second, we should simulate the movement of each bacterium one step at a time, updating their positions and directions accordingly. This approach will allow us to detect collisions more accurately and avoid the issues with bacteria moving out of bounds and back in. We should also keep track of the number of bacteria on the trap for each second, ending the simulation when all bacteria reach the trap.",
