        "thought_text": "The current approach using a time-step based simulation is on the right track, but it needs to be refined to handle the simultaneous movement of bacteria more accurately. Instead of updating all bacteria states before checking for collisions, we should simulate the movement of each bacterium one step at a time, updating their positions and directions accordingly. This will allow us to detect collisions more accurately and avoid issues with bacteria moving out of bounds and back in. Additionally, we should ensure that the trap detection is performed after all bacteria have moved, and that the infinite loop detection is based on the entire state of all bacteria, not just their positions.",
